    "created_at": "2020-07-05T17:24:23Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-07-05T17:24:23Z",
    "body": "> It would good to have what I suggested as default behavior do not you think?\r\n\r\nPersonally, I don't think changing the default `style_success` to red and `style_failure` to green would be a good change. I look at the current defaults like traffic lights, if the prompt character is green then I am good to go on and run a new command if it is red then I need to stop and check the last command. I think changing the defaults would be both confusing for starship's current users who are use to the current defaults and it would be a big change for users of other prompts who are migrating to starship most if not all have similar defaults. If I have misunderstood your suggestion please correct me but I don't think we would accept this change as it currently stands.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
